# Presentation

Presentation is separate from the value an expression returns. A presenter is a
**terminal** stage: it produces a renderable result rather than transforming the
value semantically, and nothing pipes out of it.

| Presenter | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `table` | rows and columns |
| `json` | structured data |
| `graph` | a graph view |
| `markdown` | document text |
| `tree` | nested structure |
| `text` | plain text |
| `value` | the value's own rendering |
| `empty` | nothing rendered |

```hql
cards
| typed RelationCard
| table
```

## A cell without a presenter

A cell that ends without a presenter uses a host default chosen by the result
type. [[hql/knowledge|Knowledge]] is excluded from that default, because its
views are equally valid and picking one silently would make a presentation
choice look like a property of the knowledge.

Rendering belongs to the host. Printing or saving is an explicit effect, and
constructing an updated [[card-type|Card]] does not itself persist a document.

## `graph` is doing two jobs

`graph` appears both as the projection from knowledge to a graph and as a view
of one. The projection is a function over values; the view is a presenter. They
are currently the same name, and separating them — or deciding they are one
thing — is unresolved. `expand` is traversal and stays distinct from both; see
[[hql/semantic-search]].

## Open

- Presenter naming, and whether one opaque `Presentation` type or named subtypes.
- Whether `graph` is the projection or the view.
- Presenter arguments — columns for `table`, depth for `tree` — and whether a
  presenter may be parameterized at all.
- Conversion between presentations, and what `HmdGraph` is as a value.

See [[pipes]] for the execution direction and [[hql/knowledge]] for the
projection this separates itself from.
